      "math_academy_id": "q-48845",
      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "For the functions $f(x)$ and $g(x),$ you are given the following data:\n\n$$\nf(2)=1,\\,{f}^{′}(2)=\\frac{1}{2},\\,g(2)=6,\\,{g}^{′}(2)=3\n$$\n\nCompute $\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})$ at $x=2.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the quotient rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})=\\frac{{f}^{′}(x)g(x)-f(x){g}^{′}(x)}{(g(x))^{2}}.\n$$\n\nAt the point where $x=2$, this gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{f(x)}{g(x)})|}_{x=2} & =\\frac{{f}^{′}(2)g(2)-f(2){g}^{′}(2)}{{g}^{2}(2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}\\cdot 6-1\\cdot 3}{{6}^{2}} \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields_complete": true,
